WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.820
Since 1990 the number
of gun deaths worldwide

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.510
has reached 6.5 million.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:10.430
Three quarters of gun deaths
occur in just 15 countries.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.080
Latin America is home
to some of the world's

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.770
most violent countries by murder rate.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.390
El Salvador, Venezuela and Guatemala

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:20.560
are the top three countries

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.830
for deaths caused by guns per population.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.890
These Latin American countries
are marred by corruption,

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:31.410
organized crime and a dysfunctional
criminal justice system

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.680
that further fuels the problem.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.280
The availability of guns
in the United States

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.980
is another concern for these countries.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:42.570
An estimated 200,000 guns
a year that were first sold

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.620
in the United States, are smuggled

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.350
over the southern border
and used in violent crimes

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.110
in Latin America and the Caribbean.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:54.290
In the Unites States, the
constitutional right to bear arms

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:58.150
has led to looser regulations
and easier access to firearms.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:01.662
This contributes to the
30,000 men, women and children

00:01:01.662 --> 00:01:03.670
who are killed with guns each year.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:07.070
Mass shootings attract the headlines,

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:10.750
but in fact these make up
only 0.2% of gun deaths.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:14.210
60% of gun related deaths
are in fact suicide.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:18.540
America's suicide rate increased by 25%

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.020
between 1999 and 2015, with nearly 45,000

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.390
taking their own lives in 2015 alone.

00:01:26.226 --> 00:01:29.000
Half of these suicides
were carried out with guns.

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:32.450
Though guns aren't the most
common method of suicide,

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.250
they are the most lethal.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.170
Other wealthy countries have far lower

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:38.050
rates of gun violence.

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:40.830
In Japan, if you want to
own a gun, you must pass

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.870
a written exam and a shooting
range test, alongside

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:47.960
a series of mental health,
drug and criminal record tests.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.960
It has virtually eradicated gun crime.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:55.700
After a mass shooting in
1996, Australia introduced

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:58.084
an effective buy back scheme of firearms.

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:01.070
In the 20 years following the ban,

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:03.800
there was an accelerated
decline in total gun deaths.

00:02:06.918 --> 00:02:10.085
But in America, the
House of Representatives

00:02:10.085 --> 00:02:14.370
has not voted on a single
measure to prevent gun violence

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:17.800
and in some states, such
as Texas, where students

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.120
at public colleges can now
carry concealed handguns,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.620
the law has actually loosened.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:26.420
Easy access to firearms
will continue to be

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.710
the main driver of America's gun deaths.

